   "title": "Advanced Grammar & Composition",
   "section": "Upper Division",
   "notes": "A maximum of 4 courses or 16 units of equivalent coursework may be taken in a full-immersion study abroad program and used toward this requirement, with approval from the major advisor. A maximum of two courses taught in English may be used toward this requirement from courses numbered FRENCH 140 - 142AC, and from one approved elective course from outside the French department.\nStudents must complete French 102 at UC Berkeley. Students who have passed the Bac may be exempt from this requirement and should contact frendept@berkeley.edu to discuss. Students who believe they have the equivalent education to be exempt from this requirement but have not taken the Back should contact frendept@berkeley.edu for information about the departmental placement exam.",
